course: dictionary
lesson: 12583
title: What is a diode?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A diode is a small electronic part in a circuit. It lets electric current flow in only one direction, like a one-way door. «The current can pass through the diode in one direction only.» That is the whole job of a diode.
explain: Think about what happens when a diode is turned the wrong way round. «The torch did not light because the diode was in backwards.» The one-way door is shut, so the current stops and the circuit does not work.
explain: A light-emitting diode, or LED, is a special kind of diode. When current passes through it in the right direction, it gives out light. LEDs use very little energy, so they are found in torches, screens and traffic lights.
fact: A diode is a small electronic part.
fact: A diode lets current flow in one direction only, like a one-way door.
fact: «The diode blocked the current because it was the wrong way round.»
fact: LED stands for light-emitting diode.
fact: «The traffic light uses LEDs because they use very little energy.»
exercise: «The diode lets the current flow one way only.» What does a diode do in a circuit? | It makes current flow in every direction at once | It stores electricity for ever | *It lets current flow in only one direction | It turns current into sound
exercise: «The torch did not light because the diode was in backwards.» Why did the circuit stop working? | The batteries were too big for the torch | The wires were made of wood | *The diode blocked the current going the wrong way | The torch was too bright
exercise: What does LED stand for? | Little energy display | *Light-emitting diode | Lamp with electric dots | Long electric drive
test: «LEDs are used in traffic lights because they use very little energy.» Why are LEDs used in traffic lights? | They only work in the dark | *They use very little energy | They make a loud noise | They are the cheapest bulbs in the world and never break
test: A diode works a bit like which everyday thing? | A window that opens both ways | *A one-way door | A revolving door | A drawer that never shuts
exam: «A light-emitting diode gives out light when current passes through it.» Which statement about an LED is true? | *It gives out light when current passes through it in the right direction | It stops all current from flowing | It only works when it is cold | It gives out sound when current passes through it
